content:
The bug was that `result_is_zero` was only assigned when `out` was zero — otherwise it kept its previous value, inferring a latch. The fix assigns it unconditionally.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input do_sub,
    input [7:0] a,
    input [7:0] b,
    output reg [7:0] out,
    output reg result_is_zero
);

    always @(*) begin
        case (do_sub)
            1'b0: out = a + b;
            1'b1: out = a - b;
            default: out = 8'h00;
        endcase

        result_is_zero = (out == 8'h00);
    end

endmodule
```
